## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a multi‑tenant streaming pipeline with strict data isolation, governance, and production reliability on GCP. It probes concrete choices across Pub/Sub, Dataflow, BigQuery, Cloud SQL, and security controls.

## Key Concepts

- Pub/Sub streaming ingestion
- Dataflow windowed processing
- Per-tenant BigQuery datasets and catalog joins
- IAM Conditions and per‑tenant service accounts
- VPC Service Controls and Private Service Connect
- DLP redaction before load
- End‑to‑end testing and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation: redact emails/phone in a record
function redact(record){
  const r = JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(record));
  r.payload = r.payload.replace(/[A-Za-z._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+\.[A-Za-z]{2,}/g,"REDACTED_EMAIL");
  r.payload = r.payload.replace(/\b\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{3}[-.\s]?\d{4}\b/g,"REDACTED_PHONE");
  return r;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle an on‑prem data source that misses a scheduled window?
- What metrics and alerts would you implement to detect cross‑tenant data leakage or schema drift?

